description:
CONTRACT AMENDMENT № 3 ON CONSULTANCY SERVICES

This Consultancy Services Contract amendment hereinafter referred to as the “Contract amendment No 3” intends to amend the contract and its amendments and entered into by and between:

Local Administrative Entities Development Agency (LODA), represented by Ms. NYINAWAGAGA Claudine Marie Solange, Director General of LODA, GISHUSHU P.O Box 7305 Kigali, e-mail: info@loda.gov.rw, hereinafter referred to as the “Client” on one part,

And

UNITED CONTRACTORS Ltd, hereinafter referred to as the “Consultant” on the other part,

Pursuant to the, Contract No. 000003/C/IRT/2023/2024/LODA signed on 17 February, 2025 between LODA and UNITED CONTRACTORS Ltd, for the Consultancy Services for Construction Supervision (CSC) for RUDP II Phase 4 Infrastructure in Six Secondary Cities and its amendments, especially in its article 22.1 “Contract Amendments”;

Basing on the letter No. 005/UCL/MD/LODA-Client/2025 of 30th October 2025 from UNITED CONTRACTORS Ltd requesting the replacement of key personnel Eng. MUHIRWA Adolphe, who resigned from his position as Assistant Resident Engineer for Rubavu District, and proposing Eng. UWAMUNGU Jean Nepo as a replacement;

Considering the Internal Memo from the SPIU/LODA Ag. Coordinator requesting approval for the replacement of the said key personnel following his resignation;

Considering the minutes of the LODA Public Tender Committee recommending the replacement of the key personnel;

NOW THE PARTIES AGREE TO AMEND THE INITIAL CONTRACT AS FOLLOWS:

ARTICLE 1: PURPOSE OF THE AMENDMENT

This Amendment has the objective the replacement of the existing key personnel Assistant Resident Engineer of Rubavu district following the resignation from the project, with the effective date of departure 05th December 2025;

ARTICLE 2: THE CHANGE OF THE KEY STAFF

The Assistant Resident Engineer (Rubavu) Eng. MUHIRWA Adolphe is replaced by Eng. UWAMUNGU Jean Nepo.

ARTICLE 3:  INCONSISTENT PROVISIONS

Except otherwise stated into this amendment No:3 other provisions in the initial contract, and amendment 1 and 2 remain into force;

ARTICLE 4: COMMENCEMENT 

This contract amendment shall come into force after the final signing of the contract amendment.

